  "slug": "gland-development-mll4-4b67",
  "summary": "Recent preprints apply single-cell, spatial and proteomic profiling to epithelial states in disease and culture models.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the use of single-cell, spatial or proteomic profiling to resolve epithelial and tissue cell states in disease and model systems, rather than a shared mechanism across the six preprints. In chronic pancreatitis, CD73 deletion in metaplastic epithelial cells worsened caerulein-induced fibrosis, immune remodeling and acinar-to-ductal change. Progerin induction in iPSC-derived alveolar epithelial-like cells amplified inflammatory and interferon responses to SARS-CoV-2 infection. Single-nucleus profiling of paired healthy endocervical and ectocervical samples mapped ten cell types and showed that sampling method shapes epithelial recovery. Spatial transcriptomics of CA19-9-positive pancreatic cancer linked four programs to survival and cell-line drug sensitivity. Proteomics of HGSC monolayer, spheroid and organoid cultures revealed genotype-linked mitochondria-ER contacts and lipid droplet clustering. An integrative analysis identified a 12-gene neuroimmune signature in HPV-associated cervical cancer progression. What is new is the emphasis on how tissue context and culture format alter inferred cell states, though these findings remain preprint observations.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
